---
// The same conversation as structured JSON messages (left) and as the linear Qwen token stream the model processes, ending where generation starts (right) (redraw of Fig 2-9).
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 344"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-mtt-title d2-mtt-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-mtt-title">From API messages to the model's token stream</title>
	<desc id="d2-mtt-desc">
		Left, the API level that developers see: two JSON messages, one with role system and content "You are an
		assistant", one with role user and content "Hello". An arrow labelled Chat Template points right. Right, the
		model level after Chat Template conversion, one linear token stream: im_start system, "You are an assistant"
		im_end, im_start user, "Hello" im_end, and im_start assistant, where the model starts generating. The im_start
		and im_end special tokens tell the model the role and boundaries of each message.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d2-mtt-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
			<path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead"></path>
		</marker>
	</defs>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">From API messages to the model's token stream</text>

	<text x="6" y="62" font-weight="700">API level</text>
	<text x="6" y="84" class="dg-sub">(what developers see)</text>
	<g class="dg-node dg-context">
		<rect x="6" y="98" width="276" height="70" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="20" y="124" class="dg-accent dg-mono" font-weight="700">"role": "system"</text>
		<text x="20" y="150" class="dg-sub">"content": "You are an assistant"</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="6" y="178" width="276" height="70" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="20" y="204" class="dg-accent dg-mono" font-weight="700">"role": "user"</text>
		<text x="20" y="230" class="dg-sub">"content": "Hello"</text>
	</g>

	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="290" y1="199" x2="382" y2="199" marker-end="url(#d2-mtt-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="336" y="187" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">Chat</text>
		<text x="336" y="226" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">Template</text>
	</g>

	<text x="392" y="62" font-weight="700">Model level</text>
	<text x="392" y="84" class="dg-sub">(after Chat Template conversion)</text>
	<g class="dg-node dg-neutral" style="font-variant-ligatures: none">
		<rect x="392" y="98" width="322" height="204" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="404" y="124" class="dg-mono" font-weight="700">&lt;|im_start|&gt;system</text>
		<text x="404" y="146" class="dg-mono">You are an assistant&lt;|im_end|&gt;</text>
		<text x="404" y="182" class="dg-mono" font-weight="700">&lt;|im_start|&gt;user</text>
		<text x="404" y="204" class="dg-mono">Hello&lt;|im_end|&gt;</text>
		<text x="404" y="240" class="dg-mono" font-weight="700">&lt;|im_start|&gt;assistant</text>
		<text x="404" y="280" class="dg-sub">(the model starts generating here)</text>
	</g>

	<text x="2" y="332" class="dg-sub">&lt;|im_start|&gt; and &lt;|im_end|&gt; tell the model each message's role and boundaries.</text>
</svg>
